  "note": "Static object and hotspot identity registry for Kitten Nest. This file is not wired into runtime yet. It exists to prevent selector reuse, hotspot ownership conflicts, decorative overlay drift, and rough patching. Detailed director writing guidance lives in docs/DIRECTOR_GUIDE.md.",
  "principles": [
    "No identity, no binding.",
    "Every interactive object must have an id and owner.",
    "Every decorative overlay that must align with room art must also have an id and coordinate owner.",
    "Every selector must have one primary owner.",
    "exclusive:true means the selector/action cannot be reused by another feature unless the identity card explicitly changes.",
    "Do not add per-feature blacklists; use ownership, exclusivity, and versioned change policy.",
    "canonicalCurrent means current official truth, not permanent immutability.",
    "Current official objects may change later through mutableWithVersion.",
    "Keep technical identity here; put long director notes in docs/DIRECTOR_GUIDE.md.",
    "Active base-image hotspots must be gated by their active room so home and coffeeCorner hotspots do not leak into each other.",
    "Notebook current-page preview and editor draft are separate states; do not auto-copy current page into the editor on render.",
    "Notebook save archives the saved/confirmed text immediately; do not delay the saved text until the next save.",
    "Powder notebook currently belongs to the home scene; its panel is home-scoped because no other scene currently opens it.",
    "CoffeeCorner lap-close is a scene variant, not a separate room; it owns its own hotspots and upper-left bubble."
